# L §8 Refusals outrank holes; E §5 step 1 (tally 2.1.7 R2, issue #141; #94; tally 2.1.8 S9, #179): pay is booked on 1
# February with its amount a hole (amt has no row at its booking cut). v2, known 1 March, measures it again and
# refuses it (its when divides by zero): a version answers a hole movement with a value or with a refusal, under cuts
# from its known, and the answer is its booking from then on: at cut 2026-06-30 the booking of 1 February is refused,
# early and late both, as one refused at its own cut (no unfulfilled line); at cut 2026-02-20 (early2) the hole stands.
# 2.1.6's refcore kept the hole; 2.1.7's refused an adjustment at v2's known, so early kept the hole.
=== m.tally
model h94
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source card "invented"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

input dday: date

input amt: money PLN

input div: int

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..

place world: outside lives 2026-01-01..

move pay: transfers
  on dday
  when 1 / div > 0
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt

ask early: bal(konto, 2026-02-15)
ask late: bal(konto, 2026-06-30)

version v1
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  dday = 2026-02-01 "c"
  div = 1 "c"
  opening[konto] = 10.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "c"

version v2
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-03-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN "c"
  replace div = 0 "c"
ask early2: bal(konto, 2026-02-15) as known 2026-02-20
=== expect
early: refused: RUN-DIV division by zero
  cut 2026-06-30
early2: ?"amt: no value" (amt)
  unfulfilled: pay
  cut 2026-02-20
late: refused: RUN-DIV division by zero
  cut 2026-06-30
